    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.speaking_prompts, $seed${"slug":"b2-a-time-you-had-to-adapt","title":"A Time You Had to Adapt","level":"B2","status":"published","sort_order":200,"metadata":{"task_type":"story","cue_keywords":[["ago","moved","internship","started","new","abroad","when i"],["difficult","hard","at first","missed","homesick","nervous","embarrassed","struggled"],["decided","started to","joined","invited","tried","turning point","got used to"],["learned","learnt","looking back","taught me","realised","realized"]],"model_answer":"A couple of years ago, I got a six-month internship at a software company in Germany. I'd never lived abroad before, so it was a huge change. At first, almost everything was difficult. I'd studied some German at university, but people spoke much faster than I expected, and I felt embarrassed every time I had to ask them to repeat something. I also really missed my family, especially at weekends, when the city was quiet and I was on my own. The turning point came after about a month. A colleague noticed I was eating lunch alone and invited me to join a group that went running every Saturday. I said yes, even though I was nervous, and slowly I started to make friends. I also decided to speak German in shops, even when I made mistakes, and it took me a while, but I got used to it. Looking back, I learned that adapting isn't about waiting until you feel comfortable. It's about doing small uncomfortable things until they become normal.","model_opening":"A couple of years ago, I got a six-month internship at a software company in Germany."},"prompt_text":"Tell the story of a time when you had to adapt to something new, such as a new country, school, job or way of living. Describe the situation, what was difficult, how you dealt with it, and what you learned from the experience.","prompt_type":"storytelling","target_duration_seconds":105,"target_grammar":"narrative tenses: past simple, past continuous, past perfect; used to","target_vocabulary":["at first","I'd never","used to","homesick","it took me a while","get used to","turning point","looking back"],"fluency_objective":"Build the story with time phrases like 'at first', 'after a few weeks' and 'by the end'.","pronunciation_objective":"Vary your speed and tone: slow down at the most difficult moment of the story to create interest.","cue_points":["the situation","what was difficult","how you dealt with it","what you learned"]}$seed$::jsonb) r
