    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.grammar_units, $seed${"slug":"b2-verbs-ing-or-to-meaning","title":"Remember, stop, try: -ing or to + verb?","level":"B2","status":"published","sort_order":200,"metadata":{},"focus_area":"verb-patterns","explanation_text":"Some verbs can be followed by -ing or by to + infinitive, but the meaning changes. remember / forget + -ing = a memory of something you did earlier: I remember locking the door. remember / forget + to = something you need to do: Remember to lock the door. stop + -ing = no longer do something: He stopped smoking. stop + to = stop one activity in order to do another: He stopped to buy water. try + -ing = do something as an experiment to see if it helps: Try restarting the laptop. try + to = make an effort to do something difficult: I tried to open the window, but it was stuck. regret + -ing = be sorry about something in the past: I regret leaving so early. regret + to = a formal way to give bad news: We regret to inform you that the flight has been cancelled. go on + -ing = continue the same activity; go on + to = do something new next.","contrast_text":"Compare: I'll never forget meeting you (a memory of the past). Don't forget to meet Daniel at the airport (a task for the future).","common_error_pattern":"Choosing -ing or to + verb by sound rather than meaning, for example 'I stopped to smoke' when you mean you gave it up.","examples_json":[{"bad":"Please remember sending me the file tonight.","good":"Please remember to send me the file tonight."},{"bad":"My father stopped to smoke ten years ago.","good":"My father stopped smoking ten years ago."},{"bad":"We regret informing you that your application was unsuccessful.","good":"We regret to inform you that your application was unsuccessful."},{"bad":"I'll never forget to visit Khiva for the first time.","good":"I'll never forget visiting Khiva for the first time."}],"tags":["gerund","infinitive","verb patterns"]}$seed$::jsonb) r
