    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.learning_content_registry_items, $seed${"service_key":"grammar","content_type":"grammar.unit","source_table":"grammar_units","source_ref":"c2-inverted-conditionals","title":"Had I known, should you need, were it not for","skill_key":"grammar","cefr_level":"C2","difficulty":0.9,"status":"published","description":"In formal English, if can be dropped from a conditional and the auxiliary moved in front of the subject. Should + subject + bare infinitive replaces if for possible but unlikely future events, especially in formal letters and instructions: Should you require further information, please contact us. Were + subject + to-infinitive replaces if in hypothetical sentences: Were the university to raise its fees, many students would leave. With be, use were alone: Were I in your position, I would decline the offer. Had + subject + past participle replaces if in third and mixed conditionals: Had we left earlier, we would have caught the train. Were it not for (present) and Had it not been for (past) mean 'without': Were it not for her help, I would be lost. Had it not been for her help, I would have failed. In the negative, not comes after the subject and is never contracted: Had I not seen it (no","subskill_keys":["grammar.accuracy","grammar.inversion","grammar.transfer"],"estimated_minutes":8,"learning_objective":"Compare: If I had known about the strike, I would have taken a taxi. Had I known about the strike, I would have taken a taxi. The meaning is the same; the second is more formal.","tags":["inversion","conditionals","formal style"],"payload_json":{"focus_area":"inversion","common_error_pattern":"Keeping if together with inversion ('If had I known'), contracting the negative ('Hadn't I known'), or adding will after should ('Should you will need').","examples":[{"bad":"If had we booked earlier, we would have got a discount.","good":"Had we booked earlier, we would have got a discount."},{"bad":"Hadn't it been for the map, we would have got lost.","good":"Had it not been for the map, we would have got lost."},{"bad":"Should you will need help, call reception.","good":"Should you need help, call reception."},{"bad":"Were the university raise its fees, many students would leave.","good":"Were the university to raise its fees, many students would leave."}]}}$seed$::jsonb) r
